{"name":"Alaskan Ice","hex":"#7e9ec2","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alaska","blocks":[{"text":"Alaska is a U.S. state located in the northwestern regions of North America. Part of the Western United States region, it is one of the two non-contiguous U.S. states, alongside Hawaii. Alaska is considered to be the northernmost, westernmost, and, longitudinally, the easternmost state in the United States. It is a semi-exclave of the U.S., bordering the Canadian territory of Yukon and the province of British Columbia to the east. It shares a western maritime border in the Bering Strait with Russia's Chukotka Autonomous Okrug, and is closer to another continent (Asia) than any other U.S. state. The Chukchi and Beaufort Seas of the Arctic Ocean lie to the north, and the Pacific Ocean to the south."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Flag_of_Alaska.svg/330px-Flag_of_Alaska.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska","wikidata":"Q797"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2008_AK_Proof.png/500px-2008_AK_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/2008_AK_Proof.png/500px-2008_AK_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2008_AK_Proof.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Russian_Sloop-of-War_Neva.jpg/500px-Russian_Sloop-of-War_Neva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Russian_Sloop-of-War_Neva.jpg/1280px-Russian_Sloop-of-War_Neva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Russian_Sloop-of-War_Neva.jpg/500px-Russian_Sloop-of-War_Neva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Russian settlement of St. Paul's Harbor, present-day Kodiak town, Kodiak Island, 1814","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARussian_Sloop-of-War_Neva.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Miners_climb_Chilkoot.jpg/500px-Miners_climb_Chilkoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Miners_climb_Chilkoot.jpg/1280px-Miners_climb_Chilkoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Miners_climb_Chilkoot.jpg/500px-Miners_climb_Chilkoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai